# Market Conditions Configuration Template
#
# Column Descriptions:
# - Scenario: Market condition scenario name
# - Date: Effective date for the scenario (YYYY-MM-DD)
# - Interest_Rate: Risk-free interest rate (annual, decimal)
# - Market_Volatility: Overall market volatility (standard deviation)
# - Liquidity_Premium: Additional yield for illiquid assets
# - Asset_Correlation: Average correlation between asset returns (0-1)
# - Stress_Probability: Probability of extreme event per day
# - FX_Rate: Foreign exchange rate multiplier (base = 1.00)
# - Collateral_Value_Index: Market value of collateral assets (base = 100)
#
# Scenario Definitions:
# - NORMAL: Standard market conditions, low volatility
# - MODERATE_STRESS: Elevated volatility, some market pressure
# - HIGH_STRESS: Significant market disruption, high correlations
# - CRISIS: Extreme conditions, potential systemic risk
#
# Parameter Ranges (typical):
# - Interest_Rate: 0.00 to 0.15 (0% to 15% annual)
# - Market_Volatility: 0.08 to 0.50 (8% to 50%)
# - Liquidity_Premium: 0.00 to 0.10 (0 to 10%)
# - Asset_Correlation: 0.20 to 0.95 (low to very high)
# - Stress_Probability: 0.001 to 0.50 (0.1% to 50% per day)
# - FX_Rate: 0.80 to 1.20 (±20% movement)
# - Collateral_Value_Index: 50 to 110 (50% to 110% of par)
#
# Usage Notes:
# - Multiple scenarios can be defined for stress testing
# - Parameters should reflect correlated market movements
# - Higher volatility typically correlates with higher correlations
# - Crisis scenarios should include multiple simultaneous shocks
